Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:29:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(word/builder): keep local and global track-revisions
 flags consistent

The Api.asc_GetLocalTrackRevisions bridge was overwritten by the setter
(typo on the assignment), so reading the flag reset the local track flag
to undefined and switched tracking off.

ApiDocument.SetAssistantTrackRevisions only touched the global flag: it
had no effect when the user had switched tracking off locally ("for me"
mode), and on restore it wrote the effective value into the global flag,
turning a local-only session into tracking for everyone. Keep both flags
and restore them exactly.

Adds QUnit tests in tests/word/js-api/api-track-revisions.js.

[upstreamable]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
